<title>UK: Prudential H1 operating profit rises 8 pct.</title>
<headline>Prudential H1 operating profit rises 8 pct.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year to June 30</p>
<p>			  (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr(pence, total)	 12.9		  vs 20.2</p>
<p> Shr(pence, operating)   15.2		  vs 15.1</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	   5.8		  vs 5.3</p>
<p> Pretax (including actual 361		  vs 499</p>
<p>investment gain)</p>
<p> Operating profit	   421		  vs 390</p>
<p>NOTE - Prudential Corp said its results were prepared in line with the EU Insurance Accounts Directive, which includes in pretax profit actual realised and unrealised investment gains.  </p>
<p> Shareholders' funds	5.21 billion     vs 4.33 billion</p>
<p> Insurance operations     203		  vs 199</p>
<p> Bank start-up costs	33		   vs nil</p>
<p> Tax charge		   114		  vs 114</p>
<p> Net taxed		    247		  vs 385</p>
<p> Retained profit	    136		  vs 285</p>
<p> Pay date		     Nov 28</p>
<p> Div registration date    Oct 3</p>
<p> Ex-div date		  n/a</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
